    {
      "id": "p0164-b005",
      "kind": "paragraph",
      "source": {
        "text": "Toby worded this line to fool players into thinking that the purple monster charges three gold pieces per ferry ride. In actuality, the purple monster gives the player three gold pieces after the ferry ride. It's a small, unexpected gag that pokes fun at veteran gamers' expectations.",
        "raw": "Toby worded this line to fool players into thinking that the purple monster\ncharges three gold pieces per ferry ride. In actuality, the purple monster gives\nthe player three gold pieces after the ferry ride. It's a small, unexpected gag\nthat pokes fun at veteran gamers' expectations.",
        "status": "corrected",
        "languages": [
          "en"
        ],
        "bbox": [
          0.29459834,
          0.28414286,
          0.89237824,
          0.34997857
        ],
        "mask_bbox": [
          0.29072568,
          0.28342857,
          0.91304947,
          0.35105
        ],
        "line_ids": [
          18,
          19,
          20,
          21
        ]
      },
      "translation": {
        "text": "Toby 故意这样写，让玩家以为紫色怪物每次渡河收三个金币。实际上，渡河后它反而会给玩家三个金币。这个小小的意外笑话，戏弄了老玩家的惯性预期。",
        "status": "draft",
        "spans": []
      },
      "annotations": [],
      "layout": {
        "bbox": [
          0.29563037,
          0.28271429,
          0.91100585,
          0.35355
        ],
